-- Fraud Act 2006 (2006 c. 35), section 11: OBTAINING SERVICES DISHONESTLY.
--
-- Section 11 covers a person who dishonestly obtains services that are made available on the basis
-- of payment, without paying (in full), knowing that is the basis, or that it might be, and
-- intending not to pay (in full).  It reaches what section 5 keeps out of sections 2 to 4: a
-- service is not "money or other property", so a person who aims at a free service is outside
-- section 2 but may be inside section 11 (finding 2 in NOTES.md).
--
-- The Act does not define "services" or "dishonest": both are facts the person states.

§ `Obtaining services dishonestly (section 11)`

-- src:94 | Obtaining services dishonestly
-- src:95 | 11 Obtaining services dishonestly
-- src:96 | (1) A person is guilty of an offence under this section if he obtains services for himself or another—
-- src:97 | (a) by a dishonest act, and
-- src:98 | (b) in breach of subsection (2).
@ref Fraud Act 2006 s 11(1) (src:96-98)
GIVEN `the case` IS AN `Obtaining services case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 11(1): the elements of the offence are made out` `the case` MEANS
        `the case`'s `obtains services for himself or another`
    AND `the case`'s `does so by a dishonest act`
    AND `section 11(2): the services are obtained in breach of subsection (2)` `the case`

-- src:99 | (2) A person obtains services in breach of this subsection if—
-- src:100 | (a) they are made available on the basis that payment has been, is being or will be made for or in respect of them,
-- src:101 | (b) he obtains them without any payment having been made for or in respect of them or without payment having been made in full, and
-- src:102 | (c) when he obtains them, he knows—
-- src:103 | (i) that they are being made available on the basis described in paragraph (a), or
-- src:104 | (ii) that they might be,
-- src:105 | but intends that payment will not be made, or will not be made in full.
@ref Fraud Act 2006 s 11(2) (src:99-105)
GIVEN `the case` IS AN `Obtaining services case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 11(2): the services are obtained in breach of subsection (2)` `the case` MEANS
        `section 11(2)(a): the services are made available on the basis that payment will be made` `the case`
    AND `section 11(2)(b): the services are obtained without payment, or without payment in full` `the case`
    AND `section 11(2)(c): knows they are, or might be, so made available, but intends not to pay in full` `the case`

@ref Fraud Act 2006 s 11(2)(a) (src:100)
GIVEN `the case` IS AN `Obtaining services case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 11(2)(a): the services are made available on the basis that payment will be made` `the case` MEANS
    `the case`'s `the services are made available on the basis that payment has been, is being or will be made for or in respect of them`

@ref Fraud Act 2006 s 11(2)(b) (src:101)
GIVEN `the case` IS AN `Obtaining services case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 11(2)(b): the services are obtained without payment, or without payment in full` `the case` MEANS
    NOT (`the case`'s `payment for the services` EQUALS `payment was made in full`)

@ref Fraud Act 2006 s 11(2)(c) (src:102-105)
GIVEN `the case` IS AN `Obtaining services case`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`section 11(2)(c): knows they are, or might be, so made available, but intends not to pay in full` `the case` MEANS
    -- Fork F6: "but intends that payment will not be made, or will not be made in full" is read
    -- as qualifying BOTH (i) and (ii), so the knowledge alternatives are joined first and the
    -- intention is required in either case.  The other reading would make every customer who
    -- knows services are paid for guilty whatever they meant to do.
        (   `the case`'s `when he obtains them, he knows that they are being made available on that basis`
         OR `the case`'s `when he obtains them, he knows that they might be made available on that basis`)
    AND `the case`'s `he intends that payment will not be made, or will not be made in full`

-- src:106 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:107 | (a) on summary conviction, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding the general limit in a magistrates’ court or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or to both);
-- src:108 | (b) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 5 years or to a fine (or to both).
@ref Fraud Act 2006 s 11(3) (src:106-108)
GIVEN place IS A Place
      `the date the offence was committed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`section 11(3): the penalty for obtaining services dishonestly` place `the date the offence was committed` MEANS
    `the penalty subsection: what may follow conviction` 5 place `the date the offence was committed`

-- Section 11(4) (Northern Ireland reads the limit as 6 months) is stated once, with its four
-- twins, in fraud-penalty.l4.
